                                   "title":  "Review: Himizu - Slant Magazine",
                                   "snippet":  "In films as diverse as his four-hour epic Love Exposure and his dark serial-killer drama Cold Fish, Sion Sono\u0027s characters struggle mightily and extravagantly through the highest of highs and the lowest of lows. Combined with his love of pushing the envelope of taste with the stories he tells, his films often play like exhausting emotional assaults, operatic in their intensity. Himizu, from ...",
